{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#258","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#258","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#258\",\"parent_revision\":\"c3ab4da9b679fdb2ae0b1ac5fcfc15e1db83a5174089d79424e4930ec65c44cf\",\"root_revision\":\"c3ab4da9b679fdb2ae0b1ac5fcfc15e1db83a5174089d79424e4930ec65c44cf\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWrap `file_metrics.py` as MCP tools. Agents could request file complexity analysis, token counts, and structured summaries. Tools: `count_tokens`, `scan_files`, `summarize_file`.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `file_metrics.py` exists in summarizer plugin | DERIVABLE | Check `plugins/summarizer/scripts/` |\\n| 2 | `file_metrics.py` supports `count`, `scan`, `--json` output | DERIVABLE | Inspect script interface |\\n| 3 | Summarizer plugin has or can add MCP infrastructure | DERIVABLE | Check `plugins/summarizer/` structure |\\n| 4 | FastMCP PEP 723 pattern established | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all information derivable from codebase inspection.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Feature. Additive only \u2014 wraps existing script as MCP. Low risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- MCP tool `count_tokens` wraps `file_metrics.py count`; accepts a file path, returns token count and encoding info\\n- MCP tool `scan_files` wraps `file_metrics.py scan`; accepts a directory path, returns per-file metrics\\n- MCP tool `summarize_file` wraps the summarization capability; accepts a file path, returns structured summary\\n- All tools registered in `plugins/summarizer/.mcp.json`\\n- FastMCP server validated with `uv run fastmcp list`\\n- Tools appear in an active session when the summarizer plugin is installed\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/summarizer/scripts/file_metrics.py` \u2014 script to wrap\\n- `plugins/summarizer/scripts/run_mcp_server.py` \u2014 new MCP server (PEP 723, FastMCP)\\n- `plugins/summarizer/.mcp.json` \u2014 MCP server registration\\n- `plugins/summarizer/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 version bump\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an agent using the summarizer plugin, I need `file_metrics.py` exposed as MCP tools so I can request token counts, file complexity analysis, and structured summaries without shell access.\\n\\n## Suggested Location\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/summarizer/mcp/server.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **summarizer: file metrics & summarization mcp** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: MCP backlog audit 2026-02-23\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"51373feb994fe7e2c7ee77bc4b9995d7950e22347753d257078c390089502683\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTBKng\"}"}